# 07: MadGraph's scan syntax: one launch, several coefficient values; the interference (NP^2==2)
# scales linearly, the squared term (04) quadratically.
# NOTE: this script used to set c8W2H2D2x1, which is class 7 and has NO diagram in
# p p > w+ w- (its lowest vertex is four-point and bosonic, so one insertion cannot
# enter a two-to-two diboson process).  It contributed exactly nothing.  Replaced with
# an operator that does contribute; see examples/studies/diboson/table.md.
# The numbers this prints are illustrative, not precision results.  At 2000 events an
# interference sample's effective statistics is the excess of positive over negative
# events, so MadGraph's quoted error is optimistic, and running several points in
# sequence through one process directory reuses the integration grid from the previous
# point.  A single point of this scan came out 4 sigma from the diboson study's row for
# the same operator for exactly those two reasons; four seeds at 3000 events agree with
# it. Use examples/studies/run_study.sh for numbers you intend to quote.
import model dim8_is
generate p p > w+ w- NP^2==2
output runs/07_ww_scan
launch runs/07_ww_scan
set nevents 2000
set hel_recycling False
set ebeam1 6800
set ebeam2 6800
set lam__2 1000
set c8q2W2Dx1 scan:[-2.0, -1.0, 1.0, 2.0]
done
